@startuml token_refresh_sequence

!theme plain

title Token Refresh Flow

autonumber

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFBD
}

actor "User Agent\n(Browser)" as UA
participant "Frontend Portal" as PORTAL
participant "Flexibility\nInformation System (FIS)\nAuth API" as AUTH
database "Database\nrefresh tokens" as DB

note over PORTAL
    The access token has expired
    (or is about to expire).
end note

PORTAL -> AUTH: POST /auth/v1/refresh\n<:cookie:> __Host-flex_session\n<:cookie:> __Host-flex_refresh
AUTH -> DB: Look up hash of refresh token
DB --> AUTH

alt refresh token is unknown or expired,\nor does not match the access token session
    AUTH --> PORTAL: HTTP 400\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_session\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_refresh
    PORTAL -> UA: Go to /#/login
else refresh token has already been used
    note over AUTH
        Reuse detected.
        The token was probably stolen.
    end note
    AUTH -> DB: Revoke the session
    AUTH --> PORTAL: HTTP 400\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_session\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_refresh
    PORTAL -> UA: Go to /#/login
else refresh token is valid
    AUTH -> DB: Mark token as used and insert\nnew token in the same session
    DB --> AUTH
    AUTH --> PORTAL: HTTP 200\nSet <:cookie:> __Host-flex_session (new)\nSet <:cookie:> __Host-flex_refresh (new)
    note over PORTAL
        The original request
        can now be retried.
    end note
end

|||
@enduml
